r would be to play F3.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing F3 removes a single tile that does not contribute to any immediate melds, allowing focus on forming the T1 Pung and other potential melds.  \nReason: The T1s in hand can form a Pung, and playing F3 simplifies the hand. With the existing W6-7-8 Chow, forming the T1 Pung creates two melds, leaving W1x2, W2, W8, T3x2, T4. A pair of W1s and potential future melds (e.g., Pung of T3s or W1s) can complete the hand.  \nAnswer: Play F3"}
